  "instructions": "## Build an AMD gaming desktop\n\nThe customer wants an **AMD Ryzen** build with a graphics card and an NVMe drive. The parts bin has more than you need, including some that do not fit: wrong sockets, the wrong memory generation, a cooler without the right bracket, and a power supply that is too small.\n\n## Do this\n\n1. Select a part, then click the slot it belongs in. The bench rejects parts that do not fit and tells you why.\n2. Fill every required slot: case, motherboard, CPU, cooler, memory, graphics card, NVMe drive and power supply.\n3. Choose a power supply with at least 25% headroom over the build's draw. The bench shows the running total.",
